<title>ISRAEL: Koor's Telrad in China telecom deal.</title>
<headline>Koor's Telrad in China telecom deal.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-04-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's Telrad, a subsidiary of Koor Industries Ltd, announced on Sunday a deal to supply China with phone network management systems.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for Telrad said China was buying a small number of the systems -- which trace network overloads and malfunctions in real time -- but was expected to purchase more in the coming year for several million dollars.</p>
<p>Telrad, which manufactures telecommunications equipment, is wholly owned by Koor, Israel's largest conglomerate.</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroom 972-3-5372211</p>
</text>
